# Can Flexible Non-Linear Modeling Tell Us Anything New about Educational Productivity?

**Authors:** Baker, Bruce D.

## Abstract
Explores whether flexible nonlinear models (including neural networks and genetic algorithms) can reveal otherwise unexpected patterns of relationship in typical school-productivity data. Applying three types of algorithms alongside regression modeling to school-level data in 183 elementary schools proves the hypothesis and reveals new directions for parameter selection. (Contains 31 references.) (MLH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ622982

